# Markdown recall, hand-labelled (#189).
#
# The precision samples are drawn from the documents edges the layer
# made; this one is drawn from what the docs say. Its population is every
# inline code span outside fenced blocks in the Markdown files the layer
# reads: 36,773 spans in the 16 repositories checked out beside alidade
# on 2026-10-08. 120 were drawn, allotted in proportion to each
# repository's count and taken in order of the SHA-256 of
# "repo|file|line|span". Each was labelled by reading its sentence and
# searching the repository:
#
#   declaration  names the declaration in "to", a node of the graph;
#   nonode       names a declaration of the repository the graph has no
#                node for;
#   test         names a test function, absent from the default graph;
#   external     names a declaration outside the repository;
#   gone         names a declaration the code no longer has;
#   unclear      a reader cannot tell which declaration, if any;
#   not          names no declaration: a command, flag, value, path,
#                route, keyword, or a file name used as a concept.
#
# Recall is the share of declaration spans whose section has a documents
# edge to "to", whatever span the edge records: the linker keeps one edge
# per section and target.
#
# Relabelled 2026-10-08 with #193: Go struct fields became nodes, so the
# two fields labelled nonode are declarations; and `Halted` and
# `Uncomparable`, labelled not after a search whose \b the regex engine
# did not honour, are a field and an unclear one of four fields.
#
# TestOracleGoCalls (scripts/oracle.sh) re-reads
# the sample for every repository checked out at its commit.
#
# Published here: the 19 of the 120 spans that are of public repositories
# (chameleon, protocompile, protoregistry, protovalidate, protowire-go). The others were labelled on in-house
# repositories and are not in this file; every figure above is of the
# whole sample.

repo {
